"comparison": "Both companies face execution risks associated with advancing manufacturing processes, but they emphasize different aspects of the financial impact. Intel highlights risks of margin pressure and asset impairments from delays and defects in new process nodes, citing a specific $3.1 billion charge in Q3 2024. In contrast, AMD explicitly links its inventory builds to the 'ramp of new products in advanced process nodes,' noting a $1.5 billion increase in inventories to support this ramp, which drove cash outflows. While Intel focuses on the downside risk of delays/defects causing write-downs, AMD discloses the capital commitment (inventory buildup) required to execute the advanced node ramp.",
