"comparison": "Both Intel and Qualcomm discuss the financial and operational implications of transitioning to new process technology nodes. Intel identifies 'development of next-generation process technologies' as a source of risk, including 'production timing delays, lower-than-anticipated manufacturing yields' and 'product defects.' Qualcomm notes that 'transitions to new generations of leading process technology nodes' are expected to 'continue to drive product cost increases from certain of our key semiconductor wafer suppliers.' While Intel focuses on the execution risks (yields/delays) and potential financial charges, Qualcomm focuses on the cost inflation passed through the supply chain during these transitions. Both confirm that node transitions are a critical, risky, and costly operational phase.",
